    "protein_name": "Disulfide oxidase DsbA (EC 1.8.4.-) (DsbA-like disulfide bond forming protein) (DsbA-like disulfide oxidase) (Membrane-anchored DsbA-like protein) (DsbA-like protein) (Mt-DsbA) (MtbDsbA)",
    "ec": [
      "1.8.4.-"
    ],
    "function": "Redox-active protein that catalyzes disulfide bond formation in newly translocated protein substrates (PubMed:24100317). It exhibits disulfide oxidase activity, but shows little or no activity as a disulfide reductase or as a disulfide isomerase (PubMed:23828196, PubMed:24100317, PubMed:24134223). In vitro, it shows disulfide bond isomerase activity and can catalyze the refolding of scrambled RNase A to form the correctly folded RNase A, albeit perhaps with low efficiency (PubMed:24100317, PubMed:24134223). It does not show any disulfide reductase activity with insulin as a substrate (PubMed:23828196, PubMed:24100317, PubMed:24134223). It is unable to oxidatively fold reduced and denatured hirudin, a potent natural inhibitor of thrombin (PubMed:24134223). DsbA donates its Cys-89-Cys-92 disulfide bond to the substrate and becomes reduced (PubMed:29784887). It is then re-oxidized by its redox partner, the vitamin K epoxide reductase homolog (VKOR), to start a new catalytic cycle (PubMed:29784887)..",
    "go": [
